==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=go}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sent- (go)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|senden}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sendan|t=to send, cause to go}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*sandijan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sandijaną}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro||*sont-eye-ti|t=to cause to go}}, causative of {{m|ine-pro|*sent-|t=to walk, travel}}. The noun derives from the verb.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|stq|seende|t=to send}}, {{cog|nl|zenden|t=to send}}, {{cog|de|senden|t=to send}}, {{cog|da,nb|sende|t=to send}}, {{cog|fo,is,nn|senda|t=to send}}, {{cog|sv|sända|t=to send}}. Related also to {{cog|ang|sand}}, {{m|ang|sond|t=a sending, mission, message}}. See also [[sith]].
{{col-bottom}}

